        "content": "# EnergyGrid Owner Email (single attempt)\n- PROBE answers readiness, the sender account and the recipient hash. It never reaches the Gmail node.\n- SEND renders the fixed templates, refuses a render digest mismatch, checks and writes the claim, then sends once.\n- The claim lookup and insert are NOT one atomic operation: secondary evidence only. The EnergyGrid Core seal is the authority.\n- Gmail has no retry and no attribution. An error or a lost answer is uncertain and is never resent.\n\n## Required manual configuration:\n\n- **Validate Email Request**\n  - `SUBJECT_PREFIX`: the same subject prefix as the private EnergyGrid config.\n  - `RECIPIENT`: the one owner recipient of the private EnergyGrid config.\n- **Find Existing Claim**, **Insert Claim**, **Mark Claim Sent**, **Mark Claim Uncertain**\n  - `Data table`: the EnergyGrid email claim table (string columns notificationId, dispatchId, state).\n- No workflow-level error workflow: every failure answers the Core, which owns owner visibility.",
        "width": 760,
        "height": 380
      }
    }
